\b 3. Login/Register Workflow\b0\line
\b Frontend flow\b0\line
1. User opens /login or /register.\line
2. Form submits to Next.js server action.\line
3. Server action calls platform API.\line
4. On success, frontend stores session token in cookie.\line
5. User is redirected to /dashboard.\line
\line
\b Main frontend files\b0\line
- apps/frontend/app/login/page.tsx\line
- apps/frontend/app/register/page.tsx\line
- apps/frontend/app/actions/auth.ts\line
- apps/frontend/components/auth/login-form.tsx\line
- apps/frontend/components/auth/register-form.tsx\line
- apps/frontend/lib/auth.ts\line
\line
\b Backend flow\b0\line
1. POST /api/auth/register creates account, user, subscription.\line
2. POST /api/auth/login verifies password and updates lastLogin.\line
3. API issues opaque bearer session token.\line
4. Session is stored in Redis.\line
5. Protected routes use the session token to identify account/user.\line
\line
\b Main backend files\b0\line
- apps/api/src/auth/auth.controller.ts\line
- apps/api/src/auth/auth.service.ts\line
- apps/api/src/auth/session-auth.guard.ts\line
- apps/api/src/auth/roles.guard.ts\line
\line
\b Important note\b0\line
Auth is currently Redis-backed session token auth, not true JWT auth.\line
\line
\b 4. Dashboard Entry Workflow\b0\line
1. User reaches a protected dashboard route.\line
2. Frontend checks cookie/session.\line
3. Frontend calls /api/auth/me.\line
4. If valid, dashboard renders.\line
5. If invalid, user is redirected to /login.\line
\line
\b Main dashboard protection files\b0\line
- apps/frontend/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx\line
- apps/frontend/lib/auth.ts\line
- apps/frontend/proxy.ts\line
\line
\b 5. Platform Integration Workflow (Target Design)\b0\line
This is how Meta/GA4/TikTok should work once built.\line
\line
1. User opens /gateways in dashboard.\line
2. User enters provider credentials, such as Meta Pixel ID and Access Token.\line
3. Frontend sends those credentials to the platform API.\line
4. Platform API checks session and account/container ownership.\line
5. Platform API stores config in PostgreSQL table gateway_configs.\line
6. Event processor receives tracking events.\line
7. Event processor loads enabled gateway configs for that account/container.\line
8. Event processor transforms internal event to provider-specific payload.\line
9. Event processor sends to Meta/GA4/TikTok external APIs.\line
10. Delivery result is logged for dashboard logs/analytics.\line
\line
\b Important distinction\b0\line
- Platform API = your NestJS backend.\line
- Meta API = Facebook external API.\line
\line
